                        


Item #:  SCP-5667

Object Class:  Euclid

Special Containment Procedures:  SCP-5667 has been breached from the facility and is currently undergoing investigation by mobile task force units. In the instance that SCP-5667 has been recontained the following procedures are to be enforced: SCP-5667 is to be contained within a standard Safe-class object container. All tests involving the consumption of SCP-5667 are to be forbidden unless permitted by O5. Any test involving the complete destruction of SCP-5667 is strictly forbidden and is not allowed to operate even with O5 permission. When interacting with SCP-5667 (directly or not) there is to be one personnel spectating the interaction. Any subject that has come into contact with SCP-5667 is to be put under evaluation immediately and questioned for symptoms of SCP-5667-2 instance formation.

In the event that a subject shows symptoms of being an SCP-5667-2 instance, the subject is to be contained within Class-E containment and put under constant surveillance. If the interactor shows no symptoms of being an SCP-5667-2 instance, the interactor is to be released from interrogation and is to carry out normal duties.

All SCP-5667-1 instances are to be contained within separate 8 ft x 6 ft x 6 ft containment units. Due to the breach of SCP-5667-1-7, all SCP-5667-1 instances are to be put through constant surveillance. All surveillance cameras within the containment units are to be checked on a weekly basis for damages. Any damages found upon the security cameras are to be immediately reported to O5. Under no circumstances are any SCP-5667-2 instances and SCP-5667/SCP-5667-1 instances to be within a 10 mile radius of each other.

Description:  SCP-5667 is an autonomous, whole grain loaf of bread. Upon being damaged, SCP-5667 will regenerate damaged parts using contacting materials. When in contact with solid materials, a grey doughy substance will grow upon SCP-5667 filling and repairing any damaged areas of SCP-5667. This doughy substance will then harden and take on a more bread-like structure. Further analysis of the growth will reveal it to have the same chemical makeup as whatever material SCP-5667 was in physical contact with during the regeneration process. This process has been referred to as “the solid repairment effect” and can take from 30 minutes to 5 hours depending on the solidity of the materials used.

When in contact with liquids, SCP-5667 will begin rapidly producing an unknown form of mold. The mold will proceed to grow upon SCP-5667 filling and repairing any damaged areas of SCP-5667. This process has been referred to as “the molditation effect”. This process can take from 10 minutes to an hour. This form of regeneration will also occur when contact between SCP-5667 and other substances become nonexistent, or if the tissue of an organism is the only material in contact with SCP-5667.

After one hour of consumption of SCP-5667, consumers will report feeling dizzy and will present flu-like symptoms. After these symptoms become present, the consumer’s organs will begin to shut down. This process can take from thirty minutes to an hour. Consumers of SCP-5667 report no pain during this process and even describe themselves as feeling “warm” and “safe”. After the consumer dies, their body will harden keeping them in whatever pose they were in before death. Immediately after the consumer dies there tissue will slowly alter until the consumer’s body has completely transformed into bread. The consumer’s skin will become bloated with several air pockets forming within their body during this process. This process can take from fifteen days to three months. After the process has been completed, a pulse will reform within the deceased consumer (designated SCP-5667-1). Despite SCP-5667-1 instances having a pulse; the instances will not move and will remain in a hibernation-type state. Instances of SCP-5667-1 possess the same regenerative properties as SCP-5667, yet pose no threat if consumed. There are twelve known instances of SCP-5667-1, but only eleven instances are currently contained.

While SCP-5667 does not commonly evoke emotions in personnel, 5% of those who interact with SCP-5667 report possessing the ability to hear and speak to SCP-5667 and report feeling “enlightened” by SCP-5667 (Any personnel who reports these emotions are designated as SCP-5667-2 instances). SCP-5667-2 instances will continue to hear and obsess over SCP-5667 no matter how far away or how long it has been since they have interacted with SCP-5667. SCP-5667-2 instances will continue to search for personnel to consume SCP-5667 and will continuously attempt to breach SCP-5667 from containment. Instances of SCP-5667-2 will often store SCP-5667-1 instances in a room or shelter. Attempting to enter these rooms or shelters will often result in SCP-5667-2 instances becoming hostile. After an unset amount of years, the instance of SCP-5667-2 will proceed to consume SCP-5667; turning themselves into an instance of SCP-5667-1. There have only been nine recorded instances of SCP-5667-2.



