Addendum-5667-1:  Discovery

SCP-5667 was first discovered in █/██/1973 in █████████, Florida. SCP-5667 came to the foundation’s attention after several disappearances had been reported within the area. SCP-5667-2-1 and SCP-5667 were found on ███ ███████ Rd. in a single-wide mobile home. During the containment of SCP-5667, SCP-5667-2-1 made attempts to attack the MTF epsilon 6 units but was terminated in the process. SCP-5667-2-1 was immediately hospitalized after the instance but died within Site-██ at █:██ AM, █/██/1973. Nine instances of SCP-5667-1 were found in the bedroom of the mobile home and were taken in for analysis. One civilian named [REDACTED] was also found within the mobile home bound to a metal bed frame. Subject was taken in for interrogation, administered Class-B amnestics, and released from the facility.

Addendum-5667-2:  Incidents

SCP-5667-1-7 was reported missing from its containment unit on █/██/1997. No damages could be found within the unit and all attempts to locate where SCP-5666-1-7 escaped proved futile. All surrounding security cameras showed extensive damage and all footage from █:███, █/██/1997 to █:███, █/██/1997 within the site are unavailable. The whereabouts of SCP-5667-1-7 are currently unknown and investigations are ongoing.

Dr. Evergreen (believed to be a current instance of SCP-5667-2) was spotted performing tests on SCP-5667 on █/██/1984. Testing reports show that Dr. Evergreen passed evaluation, but left the foundation one week prior to testing. SCP-5667 was reported missing on the same day as Dr. Evergreen’s resignation and it is believed Dr. Evergreen breached SCP-5667 from containment. Attempts to locate Dr. Evergreen’s whereabouts have failed. Several letters, signed under the name of “Breadcocks” (believed to be Dr. Evergreen), have been sent to the foundation with information on the events behind SCP-5667's whereabouts. (See “Addendum-5667-3”)

